{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And when you sell a sale.</b> To include movable property. And from where do we know that there is no overreaching for land? It says <b>or buy from the hand of your fellow — do not overreach</b> — a thing bought hand to hand, such as movable property, is subject to overreaching, but there is no overreaching for land." "<b>Do not overreach a man his brother.</b> [This applies] to selling a landed estate for more than its value, because it returns in the Jubilee. But if it does not return in the Jubilee there is no overreaching in it, for there is no overreaching for land."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:15:12.807962609Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}